{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 28,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.087,
            0.489,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "• 5 digit + 5 digit = 6 digit sum 60,000 + 40,000 = 1,00,000"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.124,
            0.456,
            0.14
          ],
          "content": "• 5 digit + 5 digit = 18,500"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.141,
            0.655,
            0.158
          ],
          "content": "Not possible as smallest 5-digit number is 10,000."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.158,
            0.882,
            0.192
          ],
          "content": "If both the numbers are 10,000 then the sum is 20,000, which is more than 18,500."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.196,
            0.468,
            0.246
          ],
          "content": "• 5 digit – 5 digit < 56,503 80,000 – 50,000 < 56,503 < 56,503"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.212,
            0.249,
            0.541,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": "5 digit – 3 digit = 4 digit difference 10,000 – 999 = 9001"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.212,
            0.285,
            0.54,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": "5 digit – 4 digit = 4 digit difference 12,000 – 2,500 = 9,500"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.322,
            0.54,
            0.356
          ],
          "content": "5 digit – 5 digit = 3 digit difference 50,999 – 50,000 = 999"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.359,
            0.453,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": "• 5 digit – 5 digit = 91,500"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.376,
            0.881,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": "Not possible as the difference of the greatest and the smallest 5 digit numbers, the maximum difference, can be 99,999 – 10,000 = 89,999"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.412,
            0.479,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": "Some examples of other such questions are-"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.429,
            0.425,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": "1. 5 digit + 5 digit = 7 digit sum"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.447,
            0.375,
            0.464
          ],
          "content": "2. 4 digit + 4 digit = 2900"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.465,
            0.431,
            0.482
          ],
          "content": "More such examples can be made."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.499,
            0.41,
            0.516
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Q.2. Always, Sometimes, Never?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.518,
            0.882,
            0.57
          ],
          "content": "**Below are some statements. Think, explore and find out if each of the statement is ‘Always true’, ‘Only sometimes true’ or ‘Never true’. Why do you think so? Write your reasoning; discuss this with the class.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.571,
            0.683,
            0.588
          ],
          "content": "**a. 5-digit number + 5-digit number gives a 5-digit number**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.588,
            0.684,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": "**b. 4-digit number + 2-digit number gives a 4-digit number**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.606,
            0.683,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": "**c. 4-digit number + 2-digit number gives a 6-digit number**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.624,
            0.683,
            0.641
          ],
          "content": "**d. 5-digit number – 5-digit number gives a 5-digit number**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.642,
            0.681,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": "**e. 5-digit number – 2-digit number gives a 3-digit number**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.669,
            0.358,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": "Ans. a. Only sometimes true."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.18,
            0.686,
            0.584,
            0.703
          ],
          "content": "20,000 + 80,000 = 1,00,000 not a 5 digit number"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.705,
            0.36,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": "b. Only sometimes true"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.722,
            0.528,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": "9,999 + 99 = 10,098 not a 4 digit number"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.74,
            0.276,
            0.755
          ],
          "content": "c. Never true"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.757,
            0.355,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": "9,999 + 99 = 10,098"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.775,
            0.883,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": "On adding the greatest 4 digit and the greatest 2 digit numbers, we can reach only 5 digit number 10,098. So there is no possibility of getting a 6 digit number."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.811,
            0.36,
            0.826
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "d. Only sometimes true"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.828,
            0.417,
            0.844
          ],
          "content": "Ex. 12,000 – 10,000 = 2,000"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.846,
            0.385,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "5 digit – 5 digit = 4 digit"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.864,
            0.275,
            0.879
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "e. Never true"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.881,
            0.378,
            0.897
          ],
          "content": "Ex. 10,000 – 99 = 9901"
        },
        {
